course: dictionary
lesson: 9540
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word stomach is a noun for the bag inside your body where food goes, but people also use it for the front of the body, and it can be a verb too. The words around it show you which meaning is meant. Those words are its context.
explain: «A tummy rumble is gas and liquid squeezed along the gut by its muscles, louder when the stomach is empty.» Here stomach means the bag inside you, because food and gas move through the gut. Tummy and belly are other words for the front of the body, so you can swap one in and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words only make sense as a phrase. «Butterflies in your stomach» does not mean there are insects in your tummy. It means a nervous feeling before something big. When a phrase puzzles you, do not work out each word alone: ask what the whole group of words means.
fact: Stomach is a noun: it is the bag-like organ inside your body where food is broken down.
fact: Stomach also means the front of the body below the chest, which is the tummy or belly.
fact: Stomach is a verb in «I can't stomach it», which means you can't bear it or eat it.
fact: «Butterflies in your stomach» means a nervous feeling before something big.
fact: A good check is to swap in another meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «A tummy rumble is louder when the stomach is empty.» What is the stomach here? | Something you can't bear | A kind of drink | The front of your body, like a belly | *The bag inside your body where food goes
exercise: Mia says, «I can't stomach cold porridge.» What does stomach mean here? | The front of your body, the belly | *You can't bear it or eat it | Something very cold | The bag inside your body where food is broken down
exercise: Jo says, «I have butterflies in my stomach before the test.» What does this phrase mean? | Real insects are flying in her tummy | She has eaten too much | *A nervous feeling before something big | She is hungry
test: «A cow's stomach has four chambers, an alpaca's three.» In this sentence, stomach means what? | To bear something | *The bag inside the body where food is broken down | The front of the body below the chest | A lake
test: Which phrase means a nervous feeling before something big? | Lie on your stomach | *Butterflies in your stomach | On an empty stomach | Stomach ache
exam: Ali says, «My stomach ached after I ate too much cake.» Which meaning of stomach fits? | To bear something you dislike | A kind of cake | The front of the body, the belly, but only in a painting | *The bag inside the body where food goes
